      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): handle heredoc quoting in scanTopLevelChars to prevent body content from being parsed as command stages",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #99367: Exec command display summaries parsed heredoc body content as if it were executable command stages. When a heredoc body contained `;`, `&&`, or `||`, `splitTopLevelStages` treated those as stage separators, producing misleading multi-stage summaries that showed generated file fragments (like `const slugify` or `run flutter-action@v2`) as if they were executed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`scanTopLevelChars` handled single-quote, double-quote, and backslash escaping, but did not handle heredoc (`<<`) redirects. This meant heredoc bodies were transparent to the stage/pipeline separator scanners. The fix teaches `scanTopLevelChars` to detect `<<` at the top level, parse the delimiter, and skip the entire body until the terminator line — treating it as quoted content.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Heredoc exec commands now show a clean single-stage summary like `run python3 inline script (heredoc)` instead of a confusing multi-stage chain\n- Declined heredoc command approvals no longer surface body fragments as failed sub-commands\n- Multi-stage commands with heredocs in later stages (`cd /tmp && python3 <<EOF\\n...\\nEOF`) continue to split correctly on the real separators\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [x] `pnpm test src/agents/tool-display.test.ts` — 42 tests pass\n- [x] `pnpm exec oxlint` passes on changed files\n- [x] Existing heredoc detection in `summarizeKnownExec` continues to work\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
        "branch": "fix/99367-heredoc-exec-summary",
